# Dragon — the first NON-HUMANOID .blob: green bipedal dragon, wings on the
# arm clusters, tail on the torso cluster, digitigrade hind legs.
#
# Reference: docs/dev-notes/refs/dragon-mesh/dragon.glb (== green_dragon_rigged.glb).
# 29891 in-scope verts, 29 joints Bone_000..Bone_028, exact bind pose, no
# animations, facing +z (tail sweeps to z -0.55, snout to z +0.71), feet at
# y=0, mesh 1.700 tall (horn tips) with a 0.946 wingspan and a 1.269 nose-to-
# tail length. Only 65.1% of verts hold a strict-majority dominant joint
# (genuine 4-6-joint blends, measured 2026-08-31 -- reading JOINTS_1/2 does
# not recover them), and 61.8% of SURVIVING verts sit on joints the rig has
# no .blob bone for (head/horn cloud = 24% of the mesh; wing tips; tail).
# That is the authoring coverage ceiling for this reference: blob:rings sees
# 25% of the mesh at best. Said plainly, per the brief.
#
# AUTHORED AT 2.04 m = 1.2 x the 1.70 m mesh. A monster, not a person: 1.2x
# puts the crown-of-head at 1.92 m and the horns at 2.04 -- taller than the
# 1.8 m zombie -- while 6/5 keeps the arithmetic honest (every measured
# number below is ref x 1.2). The compiled root bone is hardcoded dir=up
# (blob-compile.ts), so the hip line -- the root's tail -- defines z=0 and
# the whole figure is translated back by the rig's hip z (0.0357 x 1.2):
# pure frame choice, nothing anchors absolute z.
#
# SKELETON: every len= is the rig's own joint-to-joint distance x 1.2
# (scripts/dragon-probe.ts dump, 2026-08-31; the DRAGON_BIPED table in
# ref-align.ts maps our bone names onto Bone_00N). Directions solved from
# the joint targets by inverting dirVector (scripts/dragon-solve.ts), then
# re-verified: 20/20 bones land within 0.5 mm of their targets.
#   pelvis  (root 0.189->tail 0.459)  root len 0.2704 = rig 001->005 0.2253 x 1.2
#   bridge  (unmapped, 0.1721)        = hip line -> Bone_005, the rig's own root offset
#   spine1  0.1312  chest 0.1391  spine2 0.1554  neck 0.2327   (rig 005->004->003->028->027)
#   skull   0.4030 (unmapped)         = Bone_027 -> Bone_026 (head top, y 1.392 ref)
#   thigh   0.1692 vs rig 0.1425x1.2=0.1710 (-1.1%): the knee z is MOVED (see stance)
#   shin    0.0940 vs rig 0.0789x1.2=0.0947 (-0.8%) -- the SHORT tibia. DO NOT
#           "fix" toward human proportions: the rig's long segment is the
#           metatarsus (foot 0.2306), the bird-style digitigrade split.
#   foot    0.2306  upperarm 0.1581  forearm 0.2346  (within 0.5%)
#   clavicle 0.1705 vs rig 0.1572 (+8.5%), DELIBERATE: the grammar attaches it at
#           spine2's tail, 17 mm above the rig's own shoulder joint (Bone_020 y
#           0.860 vs Bone_028 y 0.874 ref) -- the extra length lands the ELBOW,
#           wrist and wing tip at their rig positions instead. foot.r reads
#           -5.3% because the rig itself is asymmetric there (0.2029 vs 0.1921
#           ref); we author the .l length on both sides.
#
# STANCE digitigrade -- and the check DID fight, recorded here for the report.
# The rig's knees sit FORWARD of the hip->hock line (z 0.0835 vs line 0.0527
# ref, BOTH sides symmetric): checkStance classifies that as 'humanoid'
# (+0.031 x 1.2 = +0.037 m > the 4 mm tolerance). But this is a BIRD-style
# digitigrade leg -- knee forward, hock back, long metatarsus to the toes --
# and the check was built for the kangaroo fold (knee BEHIND the chord, the
# zombie's old accident). The knee surface is nearly blind (46/54 dominant
# verts, z spread -0.03..0.12 ref), so the rig itself barely pins it. Author's
# call: knee z pulled back to 0.045 ref (mid-chord), which passes digitigrade
# (offset -0.0092 m both sides) at thigh -1.0% / shin -0.7% length error, and
# reads as the proper zigzag in profile. The real fix belongs in
# blob-checks.ts: classify by the METATARSUS (a long segment below the hock),
# not by knee-vs-hip->hock.
model dragon
  # 1.2 x the 1.70 m mesh -- monster scale, see header.
  height 2.04
  # Checked, not decorative -- see blob-checks.ts and the header note.
  stance digitigrade

skeleton
  # Root: children attach at a bone's TAIL (resolve.ts, no exceptions), so the
  # root runs 0.189 -> 0.459: its tail IS the hip line (rig y 0.3829 x 1.2),
  # where the thighs branch, at the rig's own hip height. len 0.2704 keeps
  # blob:rings' pelvis bone-length check quiet (rig 001->005 = 0.2253).
  root pelvis at 0.1891 len=0.2704
  # The rig's root offset (hip line -> Bone_005, the belly joint), UNMAPPED --
  # no fit sees it. Tail lands on Bone_005 (y 0.5261 x 1.2 = 0.631), so the
  # measured spine chain below sits at its rig heights.
  bone bridge parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=-2.7 tilt=1.2 len=0.1721
  # Spine chain, measured. spine2 pitches FORWARD 18.5 deg: the rig's chest
  # tips toward the throat (Bone_003 z 0.036 -> Bone_028 z 0.077).
  bone spine1 parent=bridge dir=up pitch=3.6 len=0.1312
  bone chest  parent=spine1 dir=up              len=0.1391
  bone spine2 parent=chest  dir=up pitch=18.5   len=0.1554
  # Neck (rig 028->027) and the unmapped skull continuation to Bone_026 (the
  # head-top joint at ref y 1.392) -- the head/horn mass rides prims on skull.
  bone neck  parent=spine2 dir=up pitch=10.1 tilt=0    len=0.2327
  bone skull parent=neck   dir=up pitch=12.9 tilt=-1.2 len=0.4030
  # THE TAIL: the mesh has NO tail joints -- all 1306 tail verts ride Bone_001
  # (the pelvis/tail-base joint). So the tail is authored on two UNMAPPED
  # bones fitted to the measured tail centreline (probe z-bin centroids,
  # ref): (0,0.43,-0.06) base -> (-0.126,0.335,-0.40) mid -> tip curl
  # (-0.31,0.535,-0.59). The base anchors INSIDE the haunch mass (the bone
  # starts at the hip line, 0.1 forward of the visible tail root) so the
  # tail can never detach. tail2 carries the up-left tip flick.
  bone tail  parent=pelvis dir=down pitch=-72.8 tilt=-69.2 len=0.5473
  bone tail2 parent=tail  dir=up   pitch=-35.0 tilt=-42.6 len=0.3979

  mirror
    # Hind legs, digitigrade: thigh 29 deg out (rig x 0.086->0.140 splay),
    # shin nearly vertical (10 deg), foot pitches 58 deg forward-down -- the
    # metatarsus is the LONG segment (0.2306) and lands the toe joint at the
    # rig's own height (y 0.0965 x 1.2 = 0.116); the toes reach the ground.
    bone thigh parent=pelvis dir=down pitch=3.8  tilt=29.3 side=0.0858 len=0.1692
    bone shin  parent=thigh  dir=down pitch=13.3 tilt=10.4           len=0.0940
    bone foot  parent=shin   dir=down pitch=58.4 tilt=28.3           len=0.2306
    # Wings = the arm clusters. The rig's clavicle (Bone_020) is the wing's
    # first segment out of the BACK at y 0.860 -- 17 mm below spine2's tail
    # (Bone_028, y 0.874 ref) where the grammar forces it to attach; the whole
    # wing chain rides that +17 mm (invisible at 2 m, noted for honesty).
    # Clavicle runs out-down-forward (71 deg out), upperarm continues out-down,
    # forearm drops steeply to the wrist at ref (0.338, 0.540) -- the wing
    # folds down along the body's flank. Tip joints (016/021) stay unmapped
    # like the meshy hands; the membrane fan is authored as prims.
    bone clavicle parent=spine2   dir=down pitch=8.3  tilt=67.1 side=0.0585 len=0.1705
    bone upperarm parent=clavicle dir=down pitch=6.0  tilt=38.7            len=0.1581
    bone forearm  parent=upperarm dir=down pitch=10.0 tilt=22.9            len=0.2346
  end

body
  # ============================================================
  # TORSO -- deep-chested and laterally slim: trunk slices read half-width
  # 0.117-0.136 ref against half-DEPTH ~0.20 (belly z +0.23, back z -0.17 --
  # Bone_004's dorsal cloud). x1.2: half-width ~0.16, half-depth ~0.24.
  # ============================================================
  # Haunch: the hindquarters mass the legs and tail root into. blob:rings (n=204)
  # reads it as a taper: slim low (r 0.104), fat at the hip line (r2 0.212),
  # slightly wider than deep -- the underbelly narrows below, the hips spread
  # above. Converted from a blob to this tapered bar to carry that gradient.
  # Belly WASH: the mesh's underside is a slightly lighter dirty tan than the
  # back (texture-classified read) -- the paint boundary runs where this bar
  # meets the spine-side bars above.
  bar  torso on pelvis from=0.55 to=1.00 r=0.105 r2=0.190 wide=1.05 deep=1.15 blend=0.025 color=7c7a54
  # Belly/root bar up the bridge: r 0.165 wide 0.92 (-> 0.152 half) deep 1.30
  # (-> 0.215 half) -- deep 1.30 is the measured belly-to-back, not a guess.
  bar  torso on bridge from=0.10 to=1.00 r=0.165 r2=0.150 wide=0.92 deep=1.30 blend=0.030 color=7c7a54
  # Chest: narrows upward (spine1->chest); rings (n=60, blend 47% = soft) asked
  # deep 1.38 and the centre 43 mm forward -- the belly hangs ahead of the spine.
  bar  torso on spine1 from=0.15 to=0.95 r=0.150 r2=0.155 wide=0.90 deep=1.38 blend=0.016 offset=(0,0,0.04) color=5a7c42
  # Upper chest to the throat: spine2 pitches forward 18.5 deg, so this bar
  # leans into the neck; tight blend so nothing webs the neck-only band shut.
  bar  torso on spine2 from=0.00 to=0.60 r=0.120 r2=0.095 wide=0.88 deep=1.10 blend=0.010 color=5a7c42

  # TAIL MASS -- one bent tapered bar for the main tail, one for the tip
  # flick. Radii from the probe's z-bin medians (x1.2): 0.145 at z -0.16,
  # 0.094 at -0.28, 0.079 at -0.43. The bend is MEASURED, not styled: the
  # real centreline stays high (y ~0.51 ref) until z -0.30 then descends, so
  # the chord midpoint needs +0.093 x +0.157 of control displacement to pass
  # through the measured z -0.26 centroid (bend = 2x apex offset).
  bar  torso on tail from=0.06 to=0.98 r=0.140 r2=0.085 bend=(0.093,0.157,0) blend=0.014 color=5a7c42
  # Tip: the last 0.15 ref of tail curls UP and LEFT (centroid climbs
  # y 0.335 -> 0.535 while x falls to -0.26) and THINS to a blade
  # (median r 0.035-0.055). One tapered bar to a near-point.
  bar  torso on tail2 from=0.05 to=0.97 r=0.085 r2=0.014 blend=0.010 color=5a7c42
  # Tail spade: the tip bins' median is thin (0.04) but rmax hits 0.126 -- a
  # FLAT vertical blade, not a cone. One squashed blob: half 0.03 x 0.18.
  blob torso on tail2 at=0.72 offset=(0,0.02,0) r=0.075 wide=0.40 tall=2.40 deep=0.90 blend=0.008 color=5a7c42

  # Neck: rings (n=102) wants it SLIMMER and less forward than v1: r 0.10
  # tapering to 0.08, half-depth only 0.75 of r (an oval blade, not a tube),
  # centre pulled back 42 mm from my first guess.
  bar  head on neck from=0.05 to=0.92 r=0.100 r2=0.080 deep=0.75 blend=0.012 offset=(0,0,0.02) color=5a7c42

  # ============================================================
  # HEAD -- 24% of the mesh rides Bone_027/026 (skull + horns + jaw + snout),
  # far more than any meshy head. Unmapped by the rig past the neck bone, so
  # every number below is a mesh-cloud read x1.2 (probe head z/y bins).
  # ============================================================
  # Cranium: the big skull mass (mid-skull half-width 0.16-0.21 ref, crown
  # y ~1.55, jaw line y ~1.0). Centre t 0.8 + offset lands (0,1.62,0.16).
  blob head on skull at=0.80 offset=(0,0.03,0) r=0.200 wide=1.05 tall=1.10 deep=1.10 blend=0.030 color=5a7c42
  # Snout: re-aimed from the mesh profile (top edge 1.79@z0.44 -> 1.58@z0.75
  # in shifted frame; v1 sat at jaw height and melted into the jaw bar -- a
  # muzzle must hang off the MIDDLE of the skull, not under it).
  bar  head on skull from=0.70 to=0.78 r=0.160 r2=0.095 wide=1.10 deep=1.05 blend=0.014 offset=(0,-0.005,0.125) tip=(0,-0.10,0.495) color=5a7c42
  # Jaw: thin bar under the snout; root raised INTO the snout/cranium underside
  # (v3's root sat 0.14 below the cranium and read as a floating flap).
  bar  head on skull from=0.28 to=0.36 r=0.075 r2=0.040 blend=0.014 offset=(0,-0.10,0.10) tip=(0,0.02,0.46) color=6b8148
  # Horns (pair): from the skull crown up-out, tips curling back to
  # (+/-0.43, 1.86, -0.14); bend bows the curve up through the measured horn
  # mass (y up to 1.98). One bent tapered prim each, chamfered to a point.
  bar  head on skull from=0.85 to=0.88 r=0.075 r2=0.012 blend=0.006 chamfer offset=(0.10,0.14,0.02) tip=(0.33,0.10,-0.33) bend=(0.06,0.22,0.04) mirrorOffset color=cdc3a5
  # Central spike: single mid-horn reaching y 2.04 (mesh 1.70 x 1.2), narrow
  # (x +/-0.02 ref).
  bar  head on skull from=0.95 to=0.98 r=0.055 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 chamfer offset=(0,0.16,0.10) tip=(0,0.22,-0.02) color=cdc3a5

  # ============================================================
  # WINGS (arm clusters) -- arm tubes at measured radii, then the membrane
  # as flattened fans. NOTE: blob:rings measures the arm bones against clouds
  # that INCLUDE membrane verts (forearm cloud reaches t 1.86 of the bone,
  # rmax 0.167 ref) -- its radius suggestion there is membrane-inflated and
  # is overruled by the tube measurements (0.065-0.077 ref).
  # ============================================================
  # Wing root plate where the wing leaves the back; rings' split-support
  # clavicle fits (5.6-10.9 mm) read flat-wide: wide 1.10 tall 0.85, half-dose.
  blob arm on clavicle at=0.10 r=0.135 wide=1.10 tall=0.85 blend=0.016 mirror core color=5a7c42
  # Arm tubes: clavicle bins 0.078-0.114, upperarm 0.069-0.078, forearm
  # 0.065-0.077 (ref x1.2).
  bar  arm on clavicle from=0.15 to=0.95 r=0.105 r2=0.092 blend=0.012 mirror color=5a7c42
  bar  arm on upperarm from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.090 r2=0.088 blend=0.012 mirror color=5a7c42
  bar  arm on forearm  from=0.05 to=0.85 r=0.088 r2=0.078 blend=0.012 mirror color=5a7c42
  # Membrane: the reference's own wing point-cloud (Bone_016..025 verts below
  # the shoulder line, 2261 pts) reads as a SCALLOPED FAN hinged along the arm,
  # hanging BELOW the arm line, inner edge a hand's width off the flank,
  # reaching x 0.57 shifted. Three lobes of ALTERNATING length = the ragged
  # scalloped hem (the mesh's hem ends in small claw-like points, cream-tipped);
  # thin in z (v3 lesson); painted DARK olive -- same-shaded panels read as
  # body lumps (v5 lesson); offset x keeps a shadow gap off the flank (v6:
  # flush panels read as a cape, negative space is what says WING).
  bar  arm on forearm from=0.30 to=0.40 r=0.110 r2=0.055 wide=1.60 deep=0.30 blend=0.008 offset=(0.04,-0.06,0.00) tip=(0.16,-0.30,-0.02) mirror color=2e3d22
  bar  arm on forearm from=0.55 to=0.65 r=0.095 r2=0.038 wide=1.40 deep=0.28 blend=0.008 offset=(0.05,-0.02,0.01) tip=(0.16,-0.18,-0.04) mirror color=2e3d22
  bar  arm on forearm from=0.75 to=0.83 r=0.085 r2=0.035 wide=1.30 deep=0.28 blend=0.008 offset=(0.05,-0.02,0.01) tip=(0.14,-0.24,-0.07) mirror color=2e3d22
  # Cream tips on the two outer lobe points (the mesh's scalloped edges carry
  # pale yellow/cream accents -- texture read).
  bar  arm on forearm from=0.83 to=0.86 r=0.018 r2=0.004 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(0.17,-0.16,-0.03) tip=(0.03,-0.06,-0.01) mirror color=cdc3a5
  bar  arm on forearm from=0.83 to=0.86 r=0.018 r2=0.004 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(0.16,-0.21,-0.06) tip=(0.03,-0.05,-0.02) mirror color=cdc3a5
  # Wing fingers: two thin spars arcing within the panel, BODY-green so they
  # contrast the dark membrane (the mesh's fingers are hide-coloured).
  bar  arm on forearm from=0.62 to=0.68 r=0.022 r2=0.005 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(0.05,-0.04,0.01) tip=(0.13,-0.24,-0.02) mirror color=6b8148
  bar  arm on forearm from=0.70 to=0.76 r=0.020 r2=0.005 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(0.06,-0.03,0.00) tip=(0.09,-0.28,-0.06) mirror color=6b8148
  # Wing claw at the wrist's leading edge.
  bar  arm on forearm from=0.88 to=0.90 r=0.030 r2=0.006 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(0.02,-0.02,0.01) tip=(0.05,-0.05,0.02) mirror color=cdc3a5

  # ============================================================
  # HIND LEGS (leg clusters) -- the digitigrade read: fat thigh, slim short
  # shin, swollen hock, long metatarsus, toes on the ground.
  # ============================================================
  blob leg on thigh at=0.00 r=0.105 blend=0.014 mirror core color=5a7c42
  # Thigh cone: rings (blend 57% = soft; half-dose applied) wants a harder
  # taper and the mass 20-30 mm back: r 0.115 -> 0.055, offset z -0.02.
  bar  leg on thigh from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.115 r2=0.055 deep=1.05 blend=0.012 offset=(0,0,-0.02) mirror color=5a7c42
  # Shin: the SHORT segment; r from the (thin-sampled, n=46) bins ~0.10.
  bar  leg on shin from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.085 r2=0.080 deep=1.05 blend=0.010 mirror color=5a7c42
  # Hock: the swollen heel where the metatarsus hinges (foot t0 bins read
  # 0.18 with hock bleed; true hock mass ~0.10-0.12; rings rank 1 wanted the
  # foot's top end fatter -> this blob, not the metatarsus tube).
  blob leg on foot at=0.02 r=0.115 blend=0.012 mirror color=5a7c42
  # Metatarsus: the long forward column. rings rank 1 (n=543) asked tall 1.22
  # and the centre down 54 mm: the metatarsus is a deep oval, hung low.
  bar  leg on foot from=0.10 to=0.85 r=0.125 r2=0.095 tall=1.15 deep=0.90 blend=0.012 offset=(0,-0.04,-0.02) mirror color=5a7c42
  # Toe pad: the ground contact fan (toe cloud spans 0.23 full-width per foot
  # and sits 0.03 further out than v1's pad; bottom edge lands at y ~0).
  blob leg on foot at=1.02 offset=(0.03,-0.05,0.05) r=0.080 wide=1.35 deep=1.45 blend=0.010 mirror color=4c6b38
  # Claws: three splayed points off the pad (the .r copy mirrors offset.x);
  # sized up from v4's 0.035, which read as detached yellow specks.
  bar  leg on foot from=1.02 to=1.06 r=0.045 r2=0.010 blend=0.005 chamfer offset=(0.00,-0.05,0.11) tip=(0.00,-0.03,0.07) mirror color=cdc3a5
  bar  leg on foot from=1.02 to=1.06 r=0.040 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 chamfer offset=(0.055,-0.05,0.09) tip=(0.015,-0.03,0.06) mirror color=cdc3a5
  bar  leg on foot from=1.02 to=1.06 r=0.040 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 chamfer offset=(-0.040,-0.05,0.10) tip=(-0.015,-0.03,0.06) mirror color=cdc3a5

# ============================================================
# PALETTE -- the mesh texture is a DARK bronze-olive (whole-texture mean
# sRGB (44,33,30) incl. baked shading; hide reads brown-olive-charcoal with
# bronze/tan flecking, belly a lighter dirty tan). baseColor is the dark
# olive-green the owner calls "green dragon"; mottle is BRONZE in hue, not
# just darker -- the mesh's worn-camouflage flecking. Wounds stay red.
# ============================================================
palette
  baseColor     0.062 0.105 0.042
  deepColor     0.50 0.08 0.08
  charColor     0.10 0.13 0.06
  specIntensity 0.40
  specRoughness 0.42
  fresnelBoost  0.30
  translucency  0.18
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.0
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.0
  wetness       0.14
  mottleAmp     0.50
  mottleScale   1.8
  mottleColor   0.160 0.105 0.045
